{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghWD6sgK4jwrkfGUxd2F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Dq ≈ 1.5 × 10³ cm⁻¹ (rough estimate). B cannot be determined from this band.**\n\n**Why B is not obtainable.** For d⁹, the ground state is ²D (octahedral ²Eg), and the only spin-allowed d–d excitation is ²Eg ← ²T2g. In a regular octahedron its energy is exactly 10Dq, so the Racah B (and C) drop out at first order. A single band therefore cannot fix B, and no value can be assigned from these data.\n\n**Why Dq is only approximate.** The complex is a six-coordinate Cu(II) with axial waters, so it is Jahn–Teller (tetragonally) distorted. The ²Eg and ²T2g levels split into several components (²B1g, ²A1g, ²Eg in D4h), and the observed envelope is a composite. With that caveat, taking the band maximum as the 10Dq-type transition gives:\n\nDq ≈ 14 720 / 10 ≈ 1470 cm⁻¹\n\nThe shoulder at 12 240 cm⁻¹ would give about 1220 cm⁻¹ on the same basis. Separating Dq from the tetragonal parameters (Ds, Dt) and obtaining B would need at least a second independent band, such as a spin-allowed transition in the d⁸-type analysis or a charge-transfer or spin-forbidden band, or a full multi-band fit.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1470, \"B\": null, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": true, \"reason\": \"A single d⁹ band (Jahn–Teller split) gives only an approximate Dq ≈ 1470 cm⁻¹ via 10Dq, and B is not determined by d⁹ band energies.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":218,"cache_read_input_tokens":1480,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":218,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"181b78e4-78a8-4055-85bb-4dfe2e128ce7","uuid":"18afdad3-312d-446d-9f7